    def html_body_text(body: str) -> str:
        """An e-mail's HTML body as the text a reader sees (karar 2026-09-29).
    
        When an Outlook message has no plain-text body, extract-msg hands over the HTML one, and it
        used to be stored as markup: `<html xmlns:v=…>`, Office `<o:p>` tags, a `<style>` block. The
        data-dump gate then read BKM correspondence as an XML pile, and the e-mails it let through
